## About this package

Ready-to-use image models for Emgu LiteRT, run with LiteRT's CompiledModel API (`Emgu.LiteRT`): each downloads its `.tflite` model and labels on first use, compiles it for the CPU or GPU, and recognizes or detects what is in an image file. It is part of the ${CPACK_PACKAGE_VERSION_MAJOR}.${CPACK_PACKAGE_VERSION_MINOR}.${CPACK_PACKAGE_VERSION_PATCH} release of Emgu LiteRT.

- `Mobilenet`: image classification, 1001 ImageNet classes
- `Inception`: flower species (an Inception model retrained on flowers)
- `CocoSsdMobilenetV1`, `CocoSsdMobilenetV3`: object detection, 80 COCO classes

These are the same models as in `Emgu.TF.Lite.Models`, which runs them with TensorFlow Lite's Interpreter API instead.

```csharp
using (var mobilenet = new Emgu.LiteRT.Models.Mobilenet())
{
    await mobilenet.Init();                      // or Init(accelerators: HwAccelerators.Gpu)
    var best = mobilenet.Recognize("grace_hopper.jpg")[0];
    Console.WriteLine($"{best.Label}: {best.Probability:P0}");
}
```

On the GPU, the outputs differ slightly from the CPU's (it computes in lower precision). The GPU needs LiteRT's GPU accelerator: the optional `${EMGU_LITERT_NUGET_ID}.Metal.runtime.macos` / `${EMGU_LITERT_NUGET_ID}.Metal.runtime.maui.macos` (Apple Silicon) or `${EMGU_LITERT_NUGET_ID}.OpenCL.runtime.maui.android` packages.

`ZImageTurbo` is text-to-image with [Z-Image-Turbo](https://huggingface.co/Tongyi-MAI/Z-Image-Turbo) (Alibaba Tongyi-MAI, 6B, Apache-2.0) on the CPU: 256x256 images from prompts of up to 24 tokens. It downloads the 13 graphs of [litert-community/Z-Image-Turbo-LiteRT](https://huggingface.co/litert-community/Z-Image-Turbo-LiteRT) (9.8 GB) and 0.78 GB of host tensors from the original checkpoint, and its first image writes 9 GB of weight caches, so it needs about 21 GB of storage; an image then takes about 23 s on an Apple M1.

```csharp
using (var zimage = new Emgu.LiteRT.Models.ZImageTurbo())
{
    await zimage.Init();                         // downloads 10.6 GB the first time
    var image = await zimage.Generate("a red apple on a wooden table, studio lighting", seed: 42);
    // image.Rgb: 256 x 256 pixels, 8-bit RGB
}
```

`PngMetadata` adds and reads text chunks (iTXt, UTF-8) in a PNG, e.g. to keep a generated image's prompt and seed in the file.

For online documentation please visit
<${NUGET_EMGU_URL}/wiki/files/emgutf/${CPACK_PACKAGE_VERSION_MAJOR}.${CPACK_PACKAGE_VERSION_MINOR}.${CPACK_PACKAGE_VERSION_PATCH}/document-lite/index.html>

## Note

To deploy Emgu LiteRT to a specific platform, you will also need to add one of the ${EMGU_LITERT_NUGET_ID}.runtime.{platform} nuget packages to your executable project, use the following link to search for an ${EMGU_LITERT_NUGET_ID}.runtime nuget packages:
<https://www.nuget.org/packages?q=${EMGU_LITERT_NUGET_ID}.runtime>
